{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wzomq4bso6xe3hfzznsrxhe33g3ufkorngprq232v5f7kfoz3viq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumerated first\n\nThe library turned out to be genuinely small — the CMake build compiles exactly one TU (`src/lib.c`, 43 lines) plus `include/lib.h`. `nm -D` on the C `.so` shows a **single** exported symbol, `dequantize_granule`; `get_bits` is `static` and therefore not part of the ABI. I grepped for `#define` across `c_src/` to rule out namespace-renaming macros — there are none, so no symbol-prefix mangling to reproduce.\n\n## Files written (in the current dir, not `c_src/`)\n\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn dequantize_granule`, with `#[repr(C)]` `bs_t` / `L12_scale_info`\n\n## C quirks deliberately preserved (not \"fixed\")\n\n- `get_bits` **advances `bs->pos` even when the limit check fails** — the mutation happens inside the `if` condition, before the early `return 0`.\n- `choff` is initialized **once, outside** the `j` loop, and toggles `576 → -558 → 576`, so `dst` walks *backwards* on odd steps. Faithfully kept rather than \"corrected\" to a sane stride.\n- `dst` advances on every band **even when `ba == 0`** (no writes, but the pointer still moves), and pointer arithmetic may run past `grbuf` — modeled with `wrapping_offset`.\n- `code % mod - mod / 2` is computed in **unsigned** and only then narrowed to `int`, preserving the wrap-around.\n- Signed/unsigned mixing in `int shl = n + s` (computed as `unsigned`, stored to `int`) reproduced exactly.\n- Shifts use `wrapping_shl`/`wrapping_shr` so pathological `bitalloc` values mirror x86 codegen instead of panicking. (I confirmed `mod` is always odd, so the `% mod` and `/ mod` can never divide by zero.)\n\n## Verification beyond \"it compiles\"\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Symbol gate: `comm -23` C-syms Rust-syms | **empty** ✅ |\n| Struct size/align/field offsets (C vs Rust) | identical (`bs_t` 16/8; `sci` 900/4, offsets 0/768/769/770/834) |\n| Differential fuzz, 240k cases × gcc `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os` | **1,200,000 cases, 0 mismatches** |\n| Exhaustive grid: `ba` 0–22 × 8 bit-alignments × `gs` −2..13 × `total_bands` 0–3 × 5 limit boundaries | **58,880 cases × 3 opt levels, 0 mismatches** |\n\nBoth harnesses `dlopen` the two `.so`s side by side and compare the **raw float bits** of a 48k-element guard-padded buffer (so stray/out-of-range writes are caught), the return value, and the post-call `bs_t` and `L12_scale_info` state. Coverage included the `ba == 0` skip path, the `ba < 17` and `ba >= 17` branches, negative and zero `group_size`, unaligned start positions, and limit values set at/below `pos` to force the `return 0` path.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (mtimes unchanged). One note on a judgement call: I set `panic = \"abort\"` in the release profile — the translated code is written to be panic-free, so this only guarantees we never unwind across the FFI boundary."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1664,"cache_read_input_tokens":32964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1664,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d78d929-1df5-4333-bbb0-844342eb9b68","uuid":"92068835-6f17-4036-b94d-7fc1907c1b01","timestamp":"2026-08-19T10:12:47.911Z"}
